    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "\\begin{align*}\n&\\quad\\text{If}\\ n \\geqslant 0, \\\\\n&\\quad\\text{then}\\ ||n + 6| = 2 - n| \\\\ \n&\\quad\\text{But}\\ 2 - n < 0, \\\\\n&\\quad\\text{Therefore there is no solution}.\n\\end{align*}\n\nIf \\(\\n i\\geqslant 0\\), then \\(|n + 6| = n + 6\\]. This is equal to \\(2 - n\\) if and only if \\(n + 6 = 2 - n\\), which is true when \\(n = -2\\).\n\nSo the answer is \\(n = \\boxed{-2}\\).",
